  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Security fix: sensitive HTTP headers are now redacted in diagnostic output.\n\n\t\t\tPreviously the Authorization header, and therefore a usable access token, was written verbatim\n\t\t\tinto the Debug level request logging emitted by CustomHttpClientHandler. Any consumer running\n\t\t\tat Debug retained usable credentials for the life of its log store.\n\n\t\t\tAuthorization, Proxy-Authorization, Cookie, Set-Cookie and common API key headers are now\n\t\t\tredacted in both request and response headers, along with any vendor-prefixed variant whose\n\t\t\tname ends in \"Authorization\". The authentication scheme and the credential length are\n\t\t\tretained, so failures remain diagnosable without exposing the credential.\n\n\t\t\tConsumers should upgrade and then review existing logs for previously captured tokens.",
